# What a `git archive` of this repository leaves out. Packagist serves the Composer package
# as GitHub's archive of the tag, so without this every `composer require` downloads all
# seven bindings and their bundled native libraries to use one of them. Composer needs
# composer.json, php/src (the sources and php/src/native), LICENSE and the READMEs.
#
# A deny-list on purpose, and `go/` is deliberately not on it: the Go module proxy builds
# the module zip with `git archive` of that directory, so an export-ignore that reached it
# would publish an empty or partial Go module. A new top-level directory that is not listed
# here only costs download size. SwiftPM clones, and every other registry gets a built
# package, so nothing else reads these attributes. They apply from the tree being archived:
# a tag made before this file existed keeps its full archive.
/.github          export-ignore
/.gitattributes   export-ignore
/.gitignore       export-ignore
/Package.swift    export-ignore
/global.json      export-ignore
/csharp           export-ignore
/java             export-ignore
/python           export-ignore
/ruby             export-ignore
/rust             export-ignore
/swift            export-ignore
/php/bench        export-ignore
/php/tests        export-ignore
/php/phpbench.json export-ignore
/php/phpcs.xml    export-ignore
/php/phpunit.xml  export-ignore
